  [10/1150] "<think>\nAlright, let's tackle this problem step by step. So, the question is about figuring out the shortest path for Carole to pass a message to Eden. She has two options: pass it to Aliza or to Oliver. I need to determine which of these two is closer in terms of the friendship graph.\n\nFirst, I'll try to visualize the graph based on the given friendships. Let me list out the connections:\n\n- Carole is friends with Reese and Oliver.\n- Reese is friends with Carole, Shawn, and Aliza.\n- Shawn is friends with Reese, Aliza, and Carole.\n- Aliza is friends with Shawn, Carole, and Eileen.\n- Eileen is friends with Aliza and Rodney.\n- Rodney is friends with Eileen and Shawn.\n- Montserrat is friends with Yitzchak and Edens.\n- Yitzchak is friends with Montserrat, Core, and Rochel.\n- Core is friends with Yitzchak, Jo, and Rees.\n- Jo is friends with Core, Yitzchak, and Ed.\n- Ed is friends with Jo, Core, and Mont.\n- Mont is friends with Ed and Yitz.\n- Yitz is friends with Core, Ed, and Mont.\n- Rees is friends with Carole, Aliza, and Core.\n- Core is friends with Rees, Yitz, and Jo.\n- Jo is friends with Core, Yitz, and Ed.\n- Ed is friends with Jo, Core, and Mont.\n- Mont is friends with Ed and Yitz.\n- Yitz is friends with Core, Ed, and Mont.\n- Shown is friends with Rees, Aliza, and Rodney.\n- Shown is also friends with Rees, Aliza, and Rodney.\n- Rodney is friends with Eileen and Shown.\n- Eileen is friends with Aliza and Rodney.\n- Aliza is friends with Eileen and Carole.\n- Carole is friends with Aliza and Oliver.\n- Oliver is friends with Carole and Ed.\n- Core is friends with Yitz, Rees, and Jo.\n- Jo is friends with Core, Yitz, and Ed.\n- Ed is friends with Jo, Core, and Mont.\n- Mont is friends with Ed and Yitz.\n- Yitz is friends with Core, Ed, and Mont.\n- Core is friends with Yitz, Rees, and Jo.\n- Jo is friends with Core, Yitz, and Ed.\n- Ed is friends with Jo, Core, and Mont.\n- Mont is friends with Ed and Yitz.\n- Yitz is friends with Core, Ed, and Mont.\n- Shown is friends with Rees, Aliza, and Rodney.\n- Shown is also friends with Rees, Aliza, and Rodney.\n- Rodney is friends with Eileen and Shown.\n- Eileen is friends with Aliza and Rodney.\n- Aliza is friends with Eileen and Carole.\n- Carole is friends with Aliza and Oliver.\n- Oliver is friends with Carole and Ed.\n\nNow, I need to find the shortest path from Carole to Eden. Let's see:\n\nOption 1: Carole -> Aliza\nFrom Aliza, who is connected? Eileen and Carole. Eileen is connected to Rodney, who is connected to Shown, who is connected to Rees, who is connected to Carole, but that's not helpful. Alternatively, Eileen is connected to Rodney, who is connected to Shown, who is connected to Aliza. Wait, that's a longer path.\n\nOption 2: Carole -> Oliver\nFrom Oliver, who is connected? Carole and Ed. So Carole -> Oliver -> Ed. That's two steps.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's a shorter path through other nodes. For example, Carole -> Rees -> Core -> Jo -> Ed. That would be four steps, which is longer than the two-step path through Oliver.\n\nAlternatively, Carole -> Rees -> Shown -> Rodney -> Eileen -> Aliza -> Carole? No, that's a cycle and longer.\n\nWait, maybe I missed something. Let me map it out properly.\n\nLooking at the connections again:\n\nCarole is directly connected to Aliza and Oliver.\n\nAliza is connected to Carole and Eileen.\n\nEileen is connected to Aliza and Rodney.\n\nRodney is connected to Eileen and Shown.\n\nShown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? No, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, no, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, no, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, no, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, no, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, no, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, no, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, no, Shown is connected to Rodney and Shown? Wait, no, Shown is connected to Rodne