-> Eileen -> Rodney. Still seven steps.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a shorter path through someone else. Let me check if Yitzchak is connected to anyone else. Yitzchak is friends with Core, Jo, Re, and Montserrat. Montserrat is friends with Yitzchak, but that's not helpful here.\n\nWait, maybe through Core? Let me see:\n\nCarole -> Oliver -> Yitzchak -> Core -> Jo -> Ed -> Eileen -> Rodney. That's seven steps.\n\nAlternatively, from Yitzchak, can she go to Core, then Core to Jo, then Jo to Ed, then Ed to Eileen, then Eileen to Rodney. That's seven steps.\n\nBut wait, is there a shorter path? Let me check if Yitzchak is connected to anyone else. Yitzchak is friends with Core, Jo, Re, and Montserrat. Montserrat is friends with Yitzchak, but that's not helpful. So no, the path through Core is the only way, which is seven steps.\n\nSo, comparing the two options:\n\n- Reese path: Carole -> Reese -> Shawn -> Rodney (3 steps)\n- Oliver path: Carole -> Oliver -> Yitzchak -> Core -> Jo -> Ed -> Eileen -> Rodney (7 steps)\n\nSo the shortest path is through Reese, which is three steps. Therefore, Carole should pass the message to Reese first.\n</think>\n\ncaroline -> reese -> shawn -> rodney reese"  correct=reese
