  [103/1150] '<think>\nAlright, let\'s tackle this problem step by step. So, the question is about figuring out the shortest path for Eileen to pass a message to Eden. Eileen wants to do this as efficiently as possible, so we need to look at the existing friendships and map out the connections.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the friends each person has to see how they\'re connected. Starting with Eileen, she\'s friends with Aliza and Rodney. So, from Eileen, the first step could be to Aliza or Rodney.\n\nIf Eileen goes to Aliza first, then from Aliza, who are her friends? Aliza is friends with Eileen, Caro琳ine, Reesee, and also with Yitzchak and Caro琳ine again. Wait, looking back, Aliza is friends with Eileen, Caro琳ine, Reesee, and Yitzchak. So from Aliza, she can reach Caro琳ine, Reesee, Yitzchak, and Eileen. But we need to get to Eden, so let\'s see where Aliza\'s friends are connected.\n\nCaro琳ine is friends with Reesee and Oliver. Reesee is connected to Caro琳ine and Shown. Shown is friends with Reesee and Aliza. Wait, but we\'re trying to get to Eden. Let me check if any of Aliza\'s friends are connected to Eden.\n\nLooking through the list, I see that Yitzchak is friends with Montserrat and Core. Core is friends with Yitzchak and Rochel. Rochel is friends with Core and Yitzchak. Yitzchak is also friends with Eden. So, from Aliza, she can go to Yitzchak, then to Eden. That would be Aliza -> Yitzchak -> Eden. That\'s two steps.\n\nNow, if Eileen goes to Rodney first, Rodney is friends with Eileen and Shown. Shown is friends with Reesee and Aliza. From Shown, we can go to Reesee or Aliza. Reesee is friends with Caro琳ine and Shown. Caro琳ine is friends with Reesee and Oliver. Oliver is friends with Caro琳ine and Edens. Wait, no, looking back, Olivers are friends with Caro琳ine and maybe others. Wait, actually, Olivers are friends with Caro琳ine and perhaps others. But in the list, Olivers are friends with Caro琳ine and also with Yitzchak? No, looking back, Olivers are friends with Caro琳ine and also with Yitzchak? Wait, no, Olivers are friends with Caro琳ine and also with Yitzchak? Let me check the list again.\n\nWait, the list says: "oliver is friends with caroline. yitzchak is friends with montserrat. corey is friends with rochel. eden is friends with montserrat. oliver is friends with eden." So, Olivers are friends with Caro琳ine and Edens. So from Shown, if Eileen goes to Rodney, then to Shown, then to Reesee, then to Caro琳ine, then to Oliver, then to Eden. That\'s five steps, which is longer than the other path.\n\nAlternatively, from Shown, Eileen can go to Aliza, then from Aliza to Yitzchak, then to Eden. Wait, but does Aliza connect to Yitzchak? Yes, because Aliza is friends with Yitzchak. So from Eileen to Rodney to Shown to Reesee to Caro琳ine to Oliver to Eden? No, that\'s longer. Alternatively, Eileen to Rodney to Shown to Aliza to Yitzchak to Eden. That\'s five steps as well.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought that from Aliza, you can go to Yitzchak, then to Eden. So that\'s two steps: Aliza -> Yitzchak -> Eden. That\'s shorter than going through Rodney. So the shortest path is Eileen -> Aliza -> Yitzchak -> Eden. But wait, the question is whether Eileen should pass to Aliza or Rodney first. So the first step is either Aliza or Rodney.\n\nBut the shortest path is through Aliza, so Eileen should pass to Aliza first. Therefore, the answer is Aliza.\n</think>\n\naliza aliza'  correct=aliza
