  [110/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Montserrat should pass the message to Yitzchak or Edene to reach Reese the fastest. Let's break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the friendships to see the connections. Montserrat is friends with Yitzchak and Edene. Yitzchak is connected to Reze, Core, and Montserrat. Reze is friends with Caro, Shae, and Aliza. Shae is friends with Aliza and Rodney. Aliza is also friends with Caro, Reze, and Yitzchak. Caro is friends with Edene and Oliver. Edene is friends with Montserrat, Jo, and Caro. Jo is friends with Core, Edene, and Yitzchak. Core is friends with Yitzchak, Jo, and Reze. Reze is also friends with Aliza. \n\nWait, I think I might have mixed up some names. Let me correct that. From the data, Yitzchak is friends with Montserrat, Core, and Reze. Reze is friends with Caro, Shae, and Aliza. Shae is friends with Aliza and Rodney. Aliza is friends with Caro, Reze, and Yitzchak. Caro is friends with Edene and Oliver. Edene is friends with Montserrat, Jo, and Caro. Jo is friends with Core, Edene, and Yitzchak. Core is friends with Yitzchak, Jo, and Reze. \n\nSo, starting from Montserrat, the options are Yitzchak or Edene. If Mont goes to Yitzchak, Yitz is connected to Reze. Reze is connected to Caro, Shae, and Aliza. From Reze, Caro is connected to Edene. So the path would be Mont -> Yitz -> Reze -> Caro -> Edene. That's four steps.\n\nIf Mont goes to Edene, Edene is connected to Jo. Jo is connected to Core. Core is connected to Reze. Reze is connected to Aliza, Shae, and Caro. From Reze, Caro is connected to Edene, but that's a loop. Alternatively, Reze is connected to Shae, who is connected to Rodney, who is connected to Aliza, who is connected to Caro. But that's longer. Alternatively, Reze is connected to Aliza, who is connected to Caro, who is connected to Edene. Wait, that's the same as the other path.\n\nWait, maybe there's a shorter path. Let me think again. From Edene, Jo is connected 