essa, then to Russell, then back to Colette. That's a cycle, but not helpful for reaching Vanessa.\n\nAlternatively, Colette is friends with Em impress, who is friends with Vanessa. So that's a two-step path: Colette -> Em impress -> Vanessa. That's shorter than going through other nodes.\n\nWait, but the question is whether Theodore should pass to Christina or Colette. So, from Theodore, Colette is directly connected, while Christina is also directly connected. So both are one step away. But the question is about the most efficient path to Vanessa.\n\nIf Theodore passes to Colette, Colette can reach Em impress, who can reach Vanessa in two steps. So the path would be Theodore -> Colette -> Em impress -> Vanessa. That's three steps.\n\nIf Theodore passes to Christina, Christina is friends with Theodor and Tiffany. If he goes to Tiffany, Tiffany is friends with Faiga and Kait. Faiga is friends with Nevaeh and Theodor. Nevaeh is friends with Kait and Toobe. Kait is friends with Nevaeh and Toobe. Toobe is friends with Kait and Russell. Russell is friends with Colette and Vanessa. So from Christina, it's a longer path: Theodore -> Christina -> Tiffany -> Faiga -> Nevaeh -> Kait -> Toobe -> Russell -> Colette -> Em impress -> Vanessa. That's 9 steps.\n\nAlternatively, from Christina, if he goes to Theodor, but that's the same as starting from Theodore. So no, that doesn't help.\n\nWait, but maybe from Christina, she's friends with Theodor, so if Theodore passes to Christina, then Christina can pass to Theodor, but that's going back. So that's not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, from Christina, she can pass to Tiffany, then to Faiga, then to Nevaeh, then to Kait, then to Toobe, then to Russell, then to Colette, then to Em impress, then to Vanessa. That's 8 steps.\n\nSo, the shortest path from Theodore to Vanessa is through Colette: Theodore -> Colette -> Em impress -> Vanessa. That's three steps.\n\nAlternatively, through Christina: Theodore -> Christina -> ... which is longer