  [210/1150] "<think>\nAlright, so I need to figure out whether Colette should pass the message to Yitta or Theodore to get it to Faiga the fastest. Let's break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, I'll map out the friendships to see the connections. Colette is friends with Yitta and Theodore. Yitta is friends with Empress and Colette, and also with Theodorus. Theodore is friends with Colette, Yitta, and Christos. Christos is friends with Theodorus and Tiffany. Tiffany is friends with Faiga and Colette, and also with Kaitlin. Kaitlin is friends with Toby and Nevaeh. Toby is friends with Kaitlin and Colette. Nevaeh is friends with Kaitlin and Colette, and also with Empress. Empress is friends with Vanessa and Colette, and also with Yitta. Vanessa is friends with Russell and Nevaeh. Russell is friends with Vanessa and Colette. So, putting this all together, Colette is connected to Yitta and Theodore. \n\nNow, I need to find the shortest path from Colette to Faiga. Let's explore both options.\n\nOption 1: Colette -> Yitta. Yitta is friends with Empress and Theodorus. Empress is friends with Vanessa and Colette, but Vanessa is friends with Russell and Nevaeh. Nevaeh is friends with Kaitlin and Colette. Kaitlin is friends with Toby and Nevaeh. Toby is friends with Colette and Kaitlin. So from Yitta, going to Empress doesn't seem helpful because Empress is connected back to Colette and Vanessa, who leads to Russell and Nevaeh, which doesn't directly connect to Tiffany. Tiffany is friends with Faiga, but that's a long way from Yitta.\n\nOption 2: Colette -> Theodore. Theodore is friends with Yitta, Christos, and Theodorus. Wait, no, Theodore is friends with Colette, Yitta, and Christos. So from Theodore, we can go to Yitta or Christos. Yitta is already connected to Empress and Colette, but that doesn't help. Christos is friends with Theodorus and Tiffany. Tiffany is friends with Faiga. So from Theodore, going to Christos, then to Tiffany, then to Faiga. That's a path of length 3: Colette -> Theodore -> Christos -> Tiffany -> Faiga.\n\nWait, but is there a shorter path? Let me check again. Colette to Theodore is one step. Theodore to Christos is two steps. Christos to Tiffany is three, and Tiffany to Faiga is four. So that's four steps. Alternatively, Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Empress, Empress to Vanessa, Vanessa to Russell, Russell to Colette. That loops back and doesn't help. Alternatively, Yitta to Theodorus, Theodorus to Christos, Christos to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. That's four steps as well.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a shorter path. Let me see. Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Theodorus, Theodorus to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. That's four steps. Alternatively, Colette to Theodore, Theodore to Theodorus, Theodorus to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. Also four steps. So both paths are the same length. But wait, is there a way to get from Colette to Faiga in three steps? Let's see. Colette to Theodore, Theodore to Theodorus, Theodorus to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. That's four steps. Or Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Empress, Empress to Vanessa, Vanessa to Russell, Russell to Colette. That's a loop. Alternatively, Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Empress, Empress to Colette. No, that's not helpful.\n\nWait, maybe I'm missing something. Let me check the connections again. Colette is friends with Yitta and Theodore. Yitta is friends with Empress and Theodorus. Theodorus is friends with Colette, Yitta, and Christos. Christos is friends with Theodorus and Tiffany. Tiffany is friends with Faiga and Colette. So from Colette, going to Theodore, then to Theodorus, then to Christos, then to Tiffany, then to Faiga. That's four steps. Alternatively, Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Theodorus, Theodorus to Christos, Christos to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. Also four steps. So both paths are the same length.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a shorter path. Let me think again. Colette to Theodore, Theodore to Theodorus, Theodorus to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. That's four steps. Or Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Empress, Empress to Vanessa, Vanessa to Russell, Russell to Colette. That's a loop. Alternatively, Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Empress, Empress to Colette. No, that's not helpful.\n\nWait, maybe I'm missing a direct connection. Let me check if any of Yitta's friends are directly connected to Faiga. Yitta is friends with Empress and Theodorus. Empress is friends with Vanessa and Colette. Vanessa is friends with Russell and Nevaeh. Russell is friends with Colette and Vanessa. Nevaeh is friends with Kaitlin and Colette. So no direct connection from Yitta to Faiga. Similarly, Theodore is friends with Theodorus, Yitta, and Christos. Theodorus is friends with Tiffany, who is friends with Faiga. So the path through Theodore is longer.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a shorter path through another route. Let me see. Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Theodorus, Theodorus to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. That's four steps. Alternatively, Colette to Theodore, Theodore to Theodorus, Theodorus to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. Also four steps. So both paths are the same length.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a way to get from Colette to Faiga in three steps. Let me think. Colette to Theodore, Theodore to Theodorus, Theodorus to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. That's four steps. Or Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Empress, Empress to Vanessa, Vanessa to Russell, Russell to Colette. No, that's a loop. Alternatively, Colette to Yitta, Yitta to Theodorus, Theodorus to Christos, Christos to Tiffany, Tiffany to Faiga. That's four steps.\n\nWait, maybe I'm overcomplicating this. Let me try to visualize the graph. Colette is connected to Yitta and Theodore. Yitta is connected to Empress and Theodorus. Theodorus is connected to Colette, Yitta, and Christos. Christos is connected to Theodorus and Tiffany. Tiffany is connected to Faiga and Colette. So from Colette, the shortest path to Faiga is through either Yitta or Theodore. Let's see:\n\nPath 1: Colette -> Yitta -> Theodorus -> Christos -> Ti