here's a connection I missed.\n\nLooking back, Hafsa is friends with Eyad and Prince. So, from Hafsa to Prince is one step. So, if Emery goes to Eyad, then to Hafsa, then to Prince. That's three steps.\n\nAlternatively, if Emery goes to Seth, then to Hafsa, then to Eyad, then to Prince. That's four steps, which is longer.\n\nWait, but Hafsa is friends with Eyad, so from Hafsa to Eyad is one step, but Eyad is friends with Hafsa, so it's a mutual connection. So, the path from Emery to Eyad to Hafsa to Prince is three steps.\n\nAlternatively, is there a way to go from Emery to Hafsa directly? No, because they aren't directly connected. So, the shortest path is through Eyad.\n\nWait, but let me check again. From Emery, she can go to Aimee or Seth.\n\nIf she goes to Aimee, she can go to Maimouna, Abdul, or Seth.\n\nFrom Maimouna, she can go to Pedro or back to Aimee.\n\nFrom Abdul, she can go to Emery or Aimee.\n\nFrom Seth, she can go to Maimouna, Aimee, or Hafsa.\n\nIf she goes to Seth, then to Hafsa, then to Eyad, then to Prince. That's four steps.\n\nAlternatively, if she goes to Aimee, then to Hafsa? No, because Aimee isn't connected to Hafsa. So, that's not possible.\n\nWait, maybe I'm missing a connection. Let me check the initial data again.\n\nLooking at the data:\n\n- Emery is friends with Aimee and Seth.\n- Aimee is friends with Emery, Maimouna, Abdul, and Seth.\n- Maimouna is friends with Aimee, Pedro, and Abdul.\n- Abdul is friends with Aimee and Maimouna.\n- Pedro is friends with Maimouna and Abdul.\n- Prince is friends with Sulaiman and Hafsa.\n- Sulaiman is friends with Prince, Emery, Connor, and Sulaiman.\n- Connor is friends with Sulaiman, Jonathan, and Connor.\n- Jonathan is friends with Connor, Maimouna, and Hafsa.\n- Hafsa is friends with Jonathan, Prince, and Eyad.\n- Eyad is friends with Hafsa and Emery.\n- Seth is friends with Emery, Maimouna, and Aimee.\n\nWait, so Hafsa is friends with Eyad and Prince. So, from Hafsa to Prince is one step.\n\nSo