  [610/1150] "<think>\nAlright, let's tackle this problem step by step. So, the question is about finding the shortest path for Yitzchak to pass a message to Sheldon. I need to figure out whether Yitzchak should send the message to Santiago or Yanki first.\n\nFirst, I'll list out all the friends each person has to map out the connections. Let's start with Yitzchak. From the given data, Yitzchak is friends with Yanki and Tessa. So, Yitzchak -> Yanki and Yitzchak -> Tessa.\n\nNow, I need to see if either of these friends is directly connected to Sheldon. Looking at the friends of Yanki, I see that Yanki is friends with Yitzchak and Sheldon. So, Yanki is directly connected to Sheldon. That means if Yitzchak sends the message to Yanki, it can reach Sheldon in one step.\n\nNext, let's check Tessa. Tessa is friends with Yitzchak and Nahla. Nahla, in turn, is friends with Sheldown. So, the path from Yitzchak to Tessa to Nahla to Sheldown would be two steps. That's longer than the path through Yanki.\n\nWait, but I should double-check if there's any other connection. For example, is there a shorter path through someone else? Let's see. Yitzchak is connected to Tessa, who is connected to Nahla, who is connected to Sheldown. So, that's three steps. But Yitzchak to Yanki to Sheldown is just two steps. So, definitely, Yanki is the shorter path.\n\nI don't think there's any other connection that could make it shorter. So, the shortest path is Yitzchak -> Yanki -> Sheldown.\n</think>\n\nThe shortest path is yitzchak -> yanki -> sheldon. yitzchak should begin by passing the message to yanki.\n\nyitzchak"  correct=yanky
