  [657/1150] '<think>\nAlright, let\'s tackle this problem step by step. So, the question is about finding the shortest path for Nahla to pass a message to Santiago. The options are whether she should go to Maria or Tessa first. \n\nFirst, I need to map out the friendships to see how they\'re connected. Let\'s list out the connections:\n\n- Nahla is friends with Sheldon, Maria, Tessa.\n- Sheldon is friends with Nahla, Yanki, Maria, Yitzchak.\n- Yitzchak is friends with Yanki, Tessa, Santiago, Noor.\n- Noor is friends with Yitzchak, Caitlin, Xusrat.\n- Caitlin is friends with Noor, Yitzchak, SANTIAGO.\n- SANTIAGO is friends with Caitlin, Yitzchak.\n- Yanki is friends with Yitzchak, Sheldon, Nahla.\n- Tessa is friends with Nahla, Yitzchak.\n- Xusrat is friends with Noor, Yitzchak.\n- Maria is friends with Nahla, Sheldon.\n- Yitzchak is also friends with SANTIAGO.\n\nWait, I think I might have mixed up some names. Let me correct that. The user wrote "santiago" and "yitzchak" as separate, but in the data, it\'s "SANTIAGO" and "Yitzchak". I\'ll assume that\'s a typo and treat them as the same person. So, Santiago is Yitzchak.\n\nNow, the goal is to find the shortest path from Nahla to Santiago. Let\'s see:\n\nOption 1: Nahla -> Maria. From Maria, she\'s friends with Nahla and Sheldon. From Sheldon, he\'s friends with Yitzchak, who is friends with Santiago. So the path would be Nahla -> Maria -> Sheldon -> Yitzchak (SANTIAGO). That\'s three steps.\n\nOption 2: Nahla -> Tessa. From Tessa, she\'s friends with Nahla and Yitzchak. From Yitzchak, she\'s friends with Santiago. So the path is Nahla -> Tessa -> Yitzchak (SANTIAGO). That\'s also two steps.\n\nWait, that can\'t be right. Because Tessa is directly connected to Yitzchak, who is directly connected to Santiago. So the path is two steps: Nahla -> Tessa -> Yitzchak.\n\nBut wait, in the data, Yitzchak is friends with Tessa, and Tessa is friends with Nahla. So from Nahla to Tessa is one step, then Tessa to Yitzchak is another, making it two steps. \n\nBut looking back, the data also shows that Yitzchak is friends with Yanki, who is friends with Sheldon, who is friends with Nahla. But that\'s a longer path. \n\nWait, no, the direct connections are more important. So the shortest path from Nahla to Santiago is either through Maria or Tessa. \n\nFrom Nahla, she can go to Maria (friend) or Tessa (friend). From Maria, she can go to Sheldon, but that\'s not Santiago. From Tessa, she can go directly to Yitzchak, who is Santiago. So the path through Tessa is shorter.\n\nWait, but in the data, Yitzchak is friends with Tessa, so the path is Nahla -> Tessa -> Yitzchak. That\'s two steps. \n\nAlternatively, Nahla -> Maria -> Sheldon -> Yitzchak is three steps. So the shortest path is through Tessa.\n\nWait, but in the data, Yitzchak is friends with Yanki, who is friends with Sheldon, who is friends with Nahla. But that\'s not necessary because there\'s a direct path through Tessa.\n\nSo the shortest path is Nahla -> Tessa -> Yitzchak. Therefore, Nahla should pass the message to Tessa first.\n</think>\n\nnahla -> tessa -> yitzchak\n\ntessa'  correct=tessa
