a, the fastest way to Santiago is through Yanki or Yitzchak. \n\nIf I go through Yanki: Sheldon -> Nahla -> Yanki -> Yitzchak -> Santiago. That\'s four steps.\n\nAlternatively, through Yitzchak: Sheldon -> Nahla -> Tessa -> Yitzchak -> Santiago. That\'s also four steps.\n\nSo, both paths through Nahla are longer than the direct path through Yanki.\n\nWait, but the question is whether Sheldon should pass the message to Nahla or Yanki first. So, the options are between two paths: one through Nahla and one through Yanki.\n\nFrom the above, the path through Yanki is shorter (3 steps) compared to the path through Nahla (4 steps). Therefore, Sheldon should pass the message to Yanki first.\n\nBut wait, let me double-check if there\'s a shorter path through Nahla. Is there any connection from Nahla to Santiago directly? No, because Nahla\'s friends are Maria, Tessa, Yanki, and Sheldon. None of them are directly connected to Santiago. So, the only way is through Yanki or Yitzchak.\n\nTherefore, the shortest path is through Yanki, which is three steps: Sheldon -> Yanki -> Yitzchak -> Santiago.\n\nSo, the correct option is "yanki".\n</think>\n\nsheldon -> yanki -> yitzchak -> santiago\n\nyanki'  correct=yanky
