o is connected to Nusrat. That's a path: Yitzchak -> Santiago -> Caitlin -> Noor -> Xinxin -> Nusrat. That's 5 steps.\n\nAlternatively, if Yitzchak goes to Yanki, Yanki is connected to Sheldrick, who is connected to Nahla, who is connected to Tessa, who is connected to Yitzchak. That's a loop. Alternatively, Sheldrick is connected to Maria, but Maria isn't connected to Nusrat. Wait, Maria is connected to Sheldrick and Nahla, but not to Nusrat. So that path doesn't help. Alternatively, from Yanki, Sheldrick can go to Yitzchak, but that's back. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe I'm missing a connection. Let me check the connections again. Yitzchak is friends with Yanki and Tessa. Tessa is friends with Nahla and Yitzchak. Nahla is friends with Sheldrick, Maria, and Tessa. Sheldrick is friends with Nahla, Yanki, and Maria. Maria is friends with Sheldrick and Nahla. Yanki is friends with Sheldrick and Yitzchak. So from Yitzchak, going to Yanki leads to Sheldrick, then to Nahla, then to Tessa, but that's back to Yitzchak. Alternatively, from Sheldrick, Maria is connected, but Maria isn't connected to Nusrat. So that path doesn't help.\n\nWait, maybe I'm missing that Nusrat is connected to Xinxin and Yaakov. Yaakov is connected to Faiga, and Xinxin is connected to Nusrat and Noor. Noor is connected to Xinxin and Caitlin. Caitlin is connected to Noor and Santiago. Santiago is connected to Yitzchak and Caitlin. So from Yitzchak, going to Santiago leads to Caitlin, who leads to Noor, who leads to Xinxin, who leads to Nusrat. That's 4 steps: Yitzchak -> Santiago -> Caitlin -> Noor -> Xinxin -> Nusrat. Wait, that's 5 steps, but maybe there's a shorter path.\n\nWait, maybe from Yitzchak to Tessa to Nahla to Sheldrick to Yanki to Sheldrick? No, that's looping. Alternatively, from Yitzchak to Tessa to Nahla to Sheldrick to Yanki to Sheldrick? No, same issue. Alternatively, from Yitzchak to Tessa to Nahla to Sheldrick to Yanki to Sheldrick? No, same problem.\n\nWait, maybe I'm overcomplicating. 