uin is connected to Malak and Ayden.\n\nMalak is connected to Joziah.\n\nSo Esmeralda -> Quin -> Malak -> Joziah: three steps.\n\nAlternatively, Quin -> Ayden -> Cam -> Isiah -> Joziah: four steps.\n\nSo both paths through Magaly and Quin are three steps. But wait, is there a way to get shorter? Let me see if any of the nodes are directly connected.\n\nEsmeralda is not directly connected to Joziah. So the shortest path is three steps.\n\nBut wait, is there a way through another node? Let me check if any other connections can make it shorter.\n\nLooking at the connections again, perhaps through another route. For example, from Quin, can she reach Joziah in two steps? No, because Quin is connected to Malak, who is connected to Joziah. So that's two steps from Quin to Joziah, but the path from Esmeralda to Quin is one step, so total three steps.\n\nSimilarly, through Magaly, it's three steps.\n\nSo both options give the same number of steps. But the question is which one is more efficient. Since both are three steps, but perhaps one is more direct.\n\nWait, maybe I missed something. Let me check the connections again.\n\nEsmeralda is friends with Ayden and Magaly.\n\nMagaly is friends with Esmeralda, Kendra, and Quin.\n\nQuin is friends with Esmeralda, Malak, and Ayden.\n\nMalak is friends with Quin, Joziah, and Ayden.\n\nSo from Esmeralda to Joziah:\n\nOption 1: Esmeralda -> Magaly -> Kendra -> Joziah.\n\nOption 2: Esmeralda -> Quin -> Malak -> Joziah.\n\nBoth are three steps. So either path is equally efficient.\n\nBut the question is which one is better. Since both are three steps, but perhaps the path through Magaly is shorter because Kendra is directly connected to Joziah, whereas through Quin, Malak is connected to Joziah. So both are three steps.\n\nWait, but maybe there's a way through another node. Let me check if any other connections can make it shorter.\n\nAlternatively, from Esmeralda to Quin to Ayden to Cam to Isiah to Joziah: that's six steps, which is l