  [1065/1150] "<think>\nAlright, let's tackle this problem step by step. So, Aidan wants to pass a message to Ruth as efficiently as possible. We need to figure out whether he should send it to Litzy or Mya first. \n\nFirst, I'll map out the friendships to see how they're connected. Let's start with Aidan. From the data, Aidan is friends with Litzy and Mya. So, Aidan can go directly to either of them. \n\nNow, looking at Mya's connections: Mya is friends with Ruth, Aidan, and Vihaan. So, if Aidan sends the message to Mya, she can then pass it to Ruth. That would be a two-step path: Aidan -> Mya -> Ruth.\n\nOn the other hand, if Aidan sends it to Litzy, Litzy is friends with Mya, Vihaan, and Journey. From Litzy, the message can go to Mya, but Mya is already connected to Ruth. Alternatively, Litzy can go to Journey, who is friends with Ruth. So, the path would be Aidan -> Litzy -> Journey -> Ruth. That's three steps.\n\nComparing both paths, the direct route through Mya is shorter. So, Aidan should send the message to Mya first to reach Ruth more efficiently.\n</think>\n\nmya -> ruth litzy\n\nmya"  correct=mya
