ends with aidan. But does aidan have any other friends? The data doesn\'t mention aidan being friends with anyone else except mya and litzy. So, from mya, passing to aidan would mean aidan is only connected to mya. So, if litzy passes to mya, and then mya passes to aidan, but aidan doesn\'t have a connection to jayceon. So that path wouldn\'t reach jayceon. Therefore, the only way from aidan is back to mya or litzy, which doesn\'t help. So, the path through mya to aidan doesn\'t lead to jayceon.\n\nAlternatively, from mya, passing to ruth. Ruth is connected to vihaan and journey. From ruth, to vihaan, then to journey, then to yechezkel, then to jayceon. That\'s also four steps: litzy -> mya -> ruth -> vihaan -> journey -> yechezkel -> jayceon. Wait, that\'s more steps. So, the path through vihaan is shorter.\n\nWait, but maybe there\'s a shorter path through mya. Let me check again. Mya is connected to ruth, aidan, and vihaan. From mya, passing to ruth, then to vihaan, then to journey, then to yechezkel, then to jayceon. That\'s five steps, which is longer than the four-step path through vihaan.\n\nAlternatively, from mya, passing to vihaan, then to journey, then to yechezkel, then to jayceon. That\'s four steps as well. So, both paths through vihaan and mya have similar lengths, but the question is whether litzy should pass to vihaan or aidan first.\n\nWait, but the question is whether litzy should pass to vihaan or aidan. So, the direct friends are vihaan and mya. Aidan isn\'t directly connected to litzy, so litzy can\'t pass directly to aidan. Therefore, the only options are vihaan or mya. But passing to mya doesn\'t lead directly to jayceon, so the path through mya is longer. Therefore, the shortest path is through vihaan.\n\nSo, the shortest path is litzy -> vihaan -> journey -> yechezkel -> jayceon. That\'s four steps, but the question is about the first step: should litzy pass to vihaan or aidan? Since aidan isn\'t a direct friend, the only option is vihaan. 